WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Why a runbook?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.290
Because the kit's weekly reads need
only Reader, but it makes one write:

3
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.186
the security initiative's assignment
at the intermediate root,

4
00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:11.538
in DoNotEnforce, from the guide's Step 9.

5
00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:15.642
That write is a plan, applied only
with the hash a reviewer approved,

6
00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:19.149
and its rollback is rehearsed
in test before production.

7
00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:23.587
The runbook has two stages: a live
test subscription, then production,

8
00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:27.712
with the same commands and each
environment's own settings file.

9
00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:32.824
Between them sits the go or no-go,
decided on the test stage's live evidence.

10
00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:36.020
None of it has been run against
a live subscription yet.
